$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 09/Bias

::EPI-W9-001::What best defines epidemiological bias? {
=Systematic error that can shift an estimate or inference away from the truth#Correct.
~Any random fluctuation#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~Intentional fraud only#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~A wide confidence interval only#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 09/Selection bias

::EPI-W9-002::People with severe symptoms are more likely to participate in a clinic-based study. What is the main bias? {
=Selection bias#Correct.
~Information bias#Classify whether the systematic difference concerns selection or measurement.
~Confounding#Classify whether the systematic difference concerns selection or measurement.
~Effect modification#Classify whether the systematic difference concerns selection or measurement.
}

::EPI-W9-003::Exposed participants with early symptoms are more likely to leave the cohort. What is the main bias? {
