$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 09/Confounding

::EPI-W9-018::What is confounding? {
=Distortion of an exposure-outcome association by a third variable related to both#Correct.
~Any measurement error#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~Any statistically significant result#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~Effect heterogeneity across subgroups#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
}

::EPI-W9-019::Variable Z causes the outcome and is associated with exposure in the source population, but is not caused by exposure. In scenario 1, what role is Z plausibly playing? {
=Confounder#Correct.
~Mediator#A pre-exposure common cause structure is compatible with confounding.
~Collider#A pre-exposure common cause structure is compatible with confounding.
~Random error#A pre-exposure common cause structure is compatible with confounding.
}

::EPI-W9-020::Variable Z causes the outcome and is associated with exposure in the source population, but is not caused by exposure. In scenario 2, what role is Z plausibly playing? {
