$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 09/Mediator collider

::EPI-W9-031::Why can adjustment for a mediator be inappropriate when estimating a total effect? {
=It can block part of the causal pathway of interest#Correct.
~It always increases sample size#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~It guarantees selection bias#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~It changes a cohort into a case-control study#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
}

::EPI-W9-032::Why can conditioning on a collider be harmful? {
=It can create a spurious association between causes of the collider#Correct.
~It always removes confounding#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~It increases sensitivity#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~It makes the outcome rare#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 09/Effect modification

::EPI-W9-033::How does effect modification differ from confounding? {
=It represents genuine variation in effect across levels of another variable rather than distortion to be removed#Correct.
~It is always a data-entry error#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~It means the sample is too small#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
~It is identical to selection bias#Review causal structure rather than statistical association alone.
}

::EPI-W9-034::An exposure has RR 1.0 in subgroup A and RR 2.5 in subgroup B after appropriate control of confounding. What should be considered? {
=Effect modification or heterogeneity#Correct.
~Automatic data deletion#Meaningfully different stratum-specific effects can indicate effect modification.
~A single common effect without checking#Meaningfully different stratum-specific effects can indicate effect modification.
~Case-control sampling bias by definition#Meaningfully different stratum-specific effects can indicate effect modification.
}

